 ## [9.14.0]
+- [AMPSDEV-373](https://ecosystem.atlassian.net/browse/AMPSDEV-373) Refuse to extract ZIP and TAR.GZ entries that would
+  resolve outside the target directory (path traversal), e.g. when unpacking `<dataPath>`/`<productDataPath>` home data
+  or installing the SDK with `atlas-update`. Effective entry paths are checked after trimming or flattening using the
+  current platform's rules for absolute paths (including drive-letter and UNC paths on Windows). Entry paths, entry
+  types and existing destination components are checked before extraction, rejecting archive links and special files
+  and preventing writes through existing symbolic links. Preflight failures leave the destination untouched; later
+  extraction failures can leave partial output. The Spring XML to Java transform also confines generated writes,
+  validates resource paths before conversion, and preserves input XML until all generated outputs are written.
